From 5350e203a85b0fed1a48e36ba485cba301b39716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:10:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] run-in-hermes-env: a faked HOME borrows the account
 tool store, like run_tests.sh

Review and post-merge cards call `scripts/run-in-hermes-env` directly from a
scratch HOME (env-cut runs, one pytest per file). Only `scripts/run_tests.sh`
decided to share the account's tool store, so every such run staged a private
toolchain (worker-7, core 99ff5b51c6: 1.68 GB private per run, 1.41 GB of it
`home/.hermes/tools`; pool workers held 27+ GiB of `tools/python-3.*` copies).

The borrow decision (account home lookup, HERMES_PM_ACCOUNT_SEED opt-out,
`scripts/tool_store_pins.py` pins check, UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR reuse) moves
from run_tests.sh into `scripts/_activation.sh` as
`hermes_borrow_account_store REPO` (plus `hermes_account_seed_enabled` and
`hermes_store_has_pins`). run_tests.sh calls it exactly where it did before.
run-in-hermes-env calls it only when a sync is due: an inherited current
environment keeps the store it was composed from, and nested calls under a
borrowing parent return at once (HERMES_RUNTIME_DIR already set). The
"borrowed Hermes root" line now goes to stderr so run-in-hermes-env's stdout
stays the command's. `activate` unsets the new library functions too.

Five whys: the pool filled with private toolchains -> each review card's
fake-HOME run-in-hermes-env provisioned its own tools/ -> run-in-hermes-env
never set HERMES_RUNTIME_DIR -> the borrow lived in run_tests.sh, not the
shared activation path -> it was written for the runner's own re-exec only.

Test (tests/scripts/test_tool_store_pins.py): a checkout whose
setup-hermes.sh only records the HERMES_RUNTIME_DIR / UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_DIR it
is provisioned with, a stub getent naming tmp/account, and an env cut to
PATH + fake HOME. For both entry points: pins match -> provisioned with
<account>/.hermes/tools and <account>/.local/share/uv/python; one pin
missing -> neither exported.
RED on base: 1 failed (the run-in-hermes-env match case), 14 passed.
GREEN: test_tool_store_pins.py + test_account_seed.py 59 passed;
test_activate_scripts / test_environment_script / test_activation_setup /
test_pm_core / test_tests_tree_layout 51 passed, 10 skipped.
Live (worker-3): `env -i HOME=<scratch>/home PATH=... bash
scripts/run-in-hermes-env bash -c 'exec "$__HERMES_TEST_PYTHON" -m pytest
tests/hermes_cli/test_worker_compute_capacity.py'` -> "borrowed Hermes root",
HERMES_RUNTIME_DIR=/home/ubuntu/.hermes/tools, 30 passed, 0.19 GB private,
no home/.hermes/tools, account tools/facts.json sha256 unchanged.

Card: t_01a1d6ded822b477
